# deps / build
node_modules/
dist/
.astro/
.pagefind/

# python
__pycache__/
*.pyc
.venv/
venv/

# never commit game artifacts
*.gba
*.sav
*.srm
*.ss[0-9]
*.bps
*.ips

# local
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
.DS_Store
.omc/
.superpowers/
CLAUDE.md

# Rendered map images: 32MB, fully deterministic from the pinned submodule
# (tools/porymap/Render.py regenerates all 966 in ~22s). Not committed pending a
# call on repo size vs build-time regeneration -- see DATA-AUDIT Q17.
public/maps/*.png

# Extracted sprites: 1,978 PNGs totalling 1,683,227 bytes (1.61 MiB) of actual content --
# one front pic and one icon per ENABLED SPECIES (596 each, not 430 dex numbers), so the
# extractor never has to decide which form is dex 386, plus 786 item icons.
# NOTE: `du -sh public/sprites` reports 7.9M, which is block-allocation slack, not size --
# these files average 850 bytes against a 4 KiB block, so ~80% of that figure is empty
# space on disk that git never stores. Use `du -sh --apparent-size` (1.7M) if you are
# re-litigating commit-vs-regenerate; content size is what costs repo weight.
# Same deal as the map images above: derived binaries that tools/sprites/Extract.py
# reproduces byte-identically from the pinned submodule, so committing them would just add
# a second copy to re-diff on every re-pin.
public/sprites/*/*.png

# Screenshots captured by tools/mgba/Capture.lua, run by hand from mGBA's GUI against a ROM
# this repo does not and will never contain (README.md:85-86). No size figure to report --
# unlike the map/sprite PNGs above, none have ever been captured on a machine that built this
# repo, and CI never can either, so there is no build step these regenerate from. Also unlike
# maps/sprites, a re-run is only as deterministic as "same savestate, same frame count" makes
# it (see Capture.lua's own docstring), not a pure function of the pinned submodule -- so a
# diff here can be a real difference, not noise, which is one more reason not to commit it.
# manifest.json is deliberately NOT covered by this rule. `data/manifest/map-manifest.json` is
# committed while public/maps/*.png above is not (decision 13) because the manifest is small,
# hand-readable JSON naming what the PNGs are, not a derived binary re-diffing on every re-pin
# -- the same distinction applies here, so once a maintainer actually captures, this manifest
# can be committed too.
public/screenshots/*.png
